{"id":"WPSS-2128-2024","cnr":"UKHC010178232024","case_no":"WPSS/2128/2024","filing":{"no":"WPSS/8323/2024","date":"2024-11-12"},"registered":"2024-11-12","next_date":"2026-11-04","decision_date":null,"stage":"ADMISSION MATTERS -35","status":"","coram":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","bench_type":"Single Bench","petitioners":[{"name":"MANISH NEGI","advocate":"K K JOSHI"},{"name":"PANKAJ NEGI","advocate":""}],"respondents":[{"name":"STATE OF UTTARAKHAND","advocate":"C.S.C."},{"name":"STATE OF UTTARAKHAND","advocate":"C.S.C."},{"name":"DIRECTOR PANCHAYATI RAJ","advocate":"C.S.C."},{"name":"UTTARAKHAND PURVA SAINIK KALYAN NIGAM LIMITED UPNL","advocate":"NEERAJ GARG"}],"acts":[{"act":"Under Article 226 of the Constituion of India","sections":"226"}],"history":[{"hearing_date":"2024-11-13","business_date":null,"purpose":"FRESH CASES FOR ADMISSION -3","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"},{"hearing_date":null,"business_date":"2025-01-08","purpose":"ORDERS ON APPLICATIONS -22","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"},{"hearing_date":null,"business_date":"2025-01-06","purpose":"ORDER MATTERS -17","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"},{"hearing_date":"2025-01-06","business_date":"2025-01-03","purpose":"ORDER MATTERS -17","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"},{"hearing_date":"2025-01-08","business_date":"2024-12-31","purpose":"ORDER MATTERS -17","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"},{"hearing_date":"2024-12-31","business_date":"2024-12-30","purpose":"ORDER MATTERS -17","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"},{"hearing_date":"2024-12-30","business_date":"2024-12-19","purpose":"ORDER MATTERS -17","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"},{"hearing_date":"2024-12-30","business_date":"2024-12-04","purpose":"ADMISSION MATTERS (TOP) -97","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"},{"hearing_date":"2024-12-04","business_date":null,"purpose":"FRESH CASES FOR ADMISSION -3","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"},{"hearing_date":"2024-12-04","business_date":"2024-11-13","purpose":"FRESH CASES FOR ADMISSION -3","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","cause_list_type":"DAILY CAUSE LIST"}],"orders":[{"date":"2024-11-13","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","kind":"order","text":"SL. \nNo Date \nOffice Notes, \nreports, orders \nor proceedings \nor directions \nand Registrar’s \norder with \nSignatures \nCOURT’S OR JUDGES’S ORDERS \n13.11.2024 WPSS No. 2128 of 2024 \nSri Rakesh Thapliyal, J.\n1. Mr. K.K. Joshi, learned counsel for the \npetitioners. \n2. Mr. Pooran Singh Bisht, Mr. Rajeev Singh Bisht, \nlearned Additional Chief Standing Counsels and Mr. \nPradeep Hairiya, learned Standing Counsel for the \nState - respondent nos.1 to 3. \n3. Mr. Neeraj Garg, learned counsel for respondent \nno.4. \n4. All the petitioners in this writ petition have been \nappointed through outsourcing agency on the post of \nJunior Assistant in Zila Panchayat, Chamoli, and \nworking since last more than ten to thirteen years. \nThey are seeking regularization in view of the \njudgment passed by the Division Bench of this Court in \nWrit Petition (PIL) No.116 of 2018, dated 12.11.2018, \nwhich was also affirmed by the Hon’ble Supreme \nCourt. \n5. For deciding the issue, as raised, it is necessary \nto ask certain instructions from the State. \n6. Let the respondents may get complete \ninstructions on the following issues:- \n“i. Whether against substantive/ sanctioned posts, \nappointments/ recruitments can be made through \noutsourcing agency? \nii. Whether the posts, which are within the purview \nof the “Uttarakhand Public Service Commission” (a \nConstitutional recruiting body), can be filled up \fthrough outsourcing agency? \niii. Whether the posts which are within the purview of \n“Uttarakhand Public Service Commission” can be \nfilled up through outsourcing agency, if ‘yes’, then \nwhether such recruitment/ appointments through \noutsourcing agency were made after due \nconsultation with the “Uttarakhand Public Service \nCommission? \niv. Whether Class II posts can also be filled up \nthrough outsourcing agency? \nv. Whether any criteria/ procedure has been \nprescribed/ followed for recruitment through \noutsourcing agencies? \nvi. Whether selections/ appointments/ recruitments \nwere made through outsourcing agencies on the \nrecommendation of the Selection Committee of \nsubject experts? \nvii. Whether any statutory rules have been framed \nfor empanelling outsourcing agencies? How many \noutsourcing agencies have been empanelled by the \nState Government, and what criteria they have \nadopted for empanelling the outsourcing agencies? \nPlace the list of empanelled outsourcing agencies. \nviii. Whether a substantive/ sanctioned post can be \nfilled up through outsourcing agency by ignoring the \nstatutory rules, which govern the recruitment? \nix. Who is the controlling and supervising authority \nover the empanelled outsourcing agencies?” \n7. List this matter on 04.12.2024. \n8. Keep this matter as part-heard. \n9. On the next date of listing, Mr. Pooran Singh \nBisht, Mr. Rajeev Singh Bisht, learned Additional Chief \nStanding Counsels and Mr. Pradeep Hairiya, learned \fStanding Counsel for the State will assist this Court.\n \n (Rakesh Thapliyal, J.)\n 13.11.2024 \nNISHANT"},{"date":"2024-12-04","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","kind":"order","text":"IN THE HIGH COURT OF UTTARAKHAND \nAT NAINITAL\nWrit Petition (SS) No. 2128 of 2024\nManish Negi and another. …….Petitioners.\nVersus\nState of Uttarakhand \nand others. ….…Respondents. \nPresent:\nMr. K.K. Joshi, learned counsel for the petitioner.\nMr. Rajeev Singh Bisht and Mr. Pooran Singh Bisht, learned Addl. CSC and Mr. Pradeep Hairiya, \nlearned Standing Counsel for the State.\nHon’ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal, J. \n1. Petitioners are working as Junior Engineers with the \nrespondent Department through outsourcing agency and most of \nthem are working since long back and are now seeking \nregularization / absorption in view of the judgment passed by \nthe Division Bench of this Court in WPPIL No. 116 of 2018 \ndecided on 12.11.2018, which was affirmed by the Hon’ble \nSupreme Court. \n2. On the previous date, certain questions were framed by this \nCourt to examine the issue of engagement of employees in \ndifferent departments through outsourcing agency. The \nquestions, as framed by this Court in paragraph 6 of order dated \n13.11.2024 are being extracted herein below:\n “6. Let the respondents may get complete instructions on \nthe following issues:-\ni. Whether against substantive/ sanctioned posts, \nappointments/ recruitments can be made through outsourcing \nagency? \f2\nii. Whether the posts, which are within the purview of the \n“Uttarakhand Public Service Commission” (a Constitutional \nrecruiting body), can be filled up through outsourcing agency? \niii. Whether the posts which are within the purview of \n“Uttarakhand Public Service Commission” can be filled up \nthrough outsourcing agency, if ‘yes’, then whether such \nrecruitment/ appointments through outsourcing agency were \nmade after due consultation with the “Uttarakhand Public \nService Commission? \niv. Whether Class II posts can also be filled up through \noutsourcing agency? \nv. Whether any criteria/ procedure has been prescribed/ \nfollowed for recruitment through outsourcing agencies? \nvi. Whether selections/ appointments/ recruitments were \nmade through outsourcing agencies on the recommendation of the \nSelection Committee of subject experts? \nvii. Whether any statutory rules have been framed for \nempanelling outsourcing agencies? How many outsourcing \nagencies have been empanelled by the State Government, and \nwhat criteria they have adopted for empanelling the outsourcing \nagencies? Place the list of empanelled outsourcing agencies. \nviii. Whether a substantive/ sanctioned post can be filled up \nthrough outsourcing agency by ignoring the statutory rules, \nwhich govern the recruitment?\nix. Who is the controlling and supervising authority over \nthe empanelled outsourcing agencies?” \n3. Subsequently, thereafter, some more questions were framed\nand one of the questions was whether without sending the \f3\nrequisition to the recruiting body for regular selection \nappointment can be made through outsourcing agency. \n4. Learned Counsels for the State, on written instructions, give \nanswer of most of the questions in “No”. What they have stated\nthat in fact, outsourcing appointments were completely \nprohibited but if the requisition is sent for regular selection and \nthere is delay in the regular selection process, then in such an \neventuality, for the time being, for the purposes of smooth \nfunctioning of the Department, instructions were issued to \nengage through outsourcing agency. In reference to this, one \nCircular of the Chief Secretary dated 29.10.2021 is also placed on \nrecord along with written instructions, which was addressed to \nthe all the Principal Secretaries, Secretaries, Secretaries Incharge \nas well as Head of the Department and the Commissioners and \nDistrict Magistrates of the State wherein certain instructions and \nguidelines were issued for engaging candidates on daily wage \nbasis, contractual, work charge, consolidated pay, part time, ad \nhoc through outsource agency. This Circular was issued in \ncontinuation of earlier Government Order dated 27.04.2018 and \n14.06.2018 wherein some more Clauses were substituted.\nParagraphs 12 of the said Government Order is being extracted \nhereinbelow:\n“12(2) संरचना�क ढ़ांचे म� सीधी भत� हेतु �ीकृत पदों के \nसापे� संिवदा / दैिनक वेतन /काय�प्रभा�रत / िनयत वेतन /\nअंशकािलक / तदथ� िनयु��यां िबना शासन की अनुमित के \nकदािप न की ज kय। पदो�ित के पदों पर पदो�ित की प्रिक्रया से \nइतर संिवदा आिद स्रोत से िनयु�� िकसी भी दशा म� न की जाय। \n�ीकृत पदों पर संगत िनयमावली के प्रािवधानों से इतर की गयी \nिनयु��यां शू� मानी जाय�गी और यिद इस प्रकार की कोई \nिनयु��यां भिव� म� की गयी तो स���त अिधकारी के िव�� \f4\nिवभागीय काय�वाही करते �ए ऐसे कािम�क को भुगतान िकए गए \nपा�रश्रिमक की वसूली स���त अिधकारी के वेतन /प�शन से की \nजायेगी।\n12(3) उ� प्र�र 12(2) म� िनिहत प्रािवधान के बावजूद यिद \nिवभागीय आव�कता के �ि�गत संिवदा अथवा आउटसोस� \nएज�सी (यथा उपनल, पी.आर.डी. अथवा िनजी सेवा प्रदाता फम�) \nके मा�म से कािम�क िनयोिजत िकए गए हों तो िन�वत् काय�वाही \nकी जायेगी :-\n(क) िवभाग �ारा सीधी भत� के �र� पदों पर यथासंभव शीघ्र \nिनयिमत चयन की प्रिक्रया पूण� करने हेतु हर संभव प्रयास िकया \nजायेगा।\n(ख) िवभाग �ारा सीधी भत� के पदों के सापे� पूव� म� यिद \nकाय�िहत को �ि�गत रखते�ए पारदश� चयन प्रिक्रया के मा�म \nसे संिवदा पर कािम�क िनयोिजत िकए गए हों तो पूव� िनयत संिवदा \nकी शत� के अनुसार संिवदा अविध का िव�ार पूव� म� िदए जा रहे \nअ�राल के साथ 01 वष� अथवा िनयिमत चयन की ितिथ , जो भी \nपहले हो, तक के िलए िवभागीय स�म प्रािध कारी का अनुमोदन \nप्रा� करते �ए िकया जा सकेगा।\n(x) िजन िवभागों म� के� पोिषत अथवा बा� सहायितत \nप�रयोजनाएं संचािलत ह� और योजना के िक्रया�यन हेतु गिठत \nसंरचना�क ढ़ाँचे म� सृिजत पदों को संिवदा से ही भरे जाने का \nप्रािवधान है, उन िवभागों म� इस प्रका र संिवदा पर िनयोिजत \nकािम�कों की संिवदा अविध का िव�ार प�रयोजना अविध अथवा \nस�क अ�राल के साथ संिवदा अनुब� म� यथा िनिद�� अविध \nजो भी पहले हो , तक के िलए िवभागीय स�म प्रािधकारी का \nअनुमोदन प्रा� करते �ए िकया जा सकेगा।\f5\n पर�ु िवभाग �ारा प�रयोजना म� सीिनयर मैनेजम�ट �र \nके पदों को छोड़कर अ� पदों पर सीधी संिवदा पर िनयोिजत \nकािम�कों को शनैः शनैः आउटसोिस�ग के मा�म से सिव�स \nकांट�े� के तहत िलए जाने का प्रयास अव� िकया जायेगा। \n(घ) िजन िवभागों म� सीधी भत� के पदों पर चयन प्रिक्रया म� हो रहे \nिवल� के �ि�गत अ��रम �वस्था के �प म� आउटसोस� \nएज�सी (यथा उपनल, पी.आर.डी. अथवा िनजी सेवा प्रदाता फम�) \nके मा�म से कािम�क िनयोिजत िकए गए हों , िवभाग �ारा \nआउटसोस� एज�सी के साथ की गयी संिवदा का िव�ार िनयिमत \nचयन अथवा स�म प्रािध कारी �ारा अनुब� अ�ग�त िनयत \nअविध, जो भी पहले हो , तक के िलए स�म प्रािधकारी के \nअनुमोदन से िकया जा सकेगा। ऐसे मामलों म�आउटसोस� एज�सी \n�ारा उपल� कराये गये कािम�कों के साथ िवभाग �ारा न तो सीधे \nअनुब� िकया जायेगा और न ही उ�� पा�रश्रिमक का भुगतान \nसीधे िकया जायेगा , वरन् िनयत प्रिक्रया के अनुसार िवभाग �ारा \nआउटसोस� एज�सी के साथ ही अनुब� करते �ए देय धनरािश का \nभुगतान आउटसोस� एज�सी को ही िकया जायेगा।“\n5. Apart from this, learned State Counsel inform to this Court \nthat the posts of Junior Engineer against which petitioners were \nappointed are in fact within the purview of the Public Service \nCommission and therefore, the posts, which are within the \npurview of the Public Service Commission, cannot be filled up \nthrough outsourcing agency. \n6. Now, the question, if the posts, which are within the \npurview of the Public Service Commission, cannot be filled \nthrough outsourcing agency, then why appointments were made \nthrough outsourcing agency. \f6\n7. Apart from this, one more question was with regard to the \nprocedure of empanelment of outsource agencies and in reply \nthereto, Mr. Rajeev Singh Bisht, learned Addl. CSC submits that \nthe is Government Order dated 11.08.2023 prescribes the \nprocedure for empanelling the outsourcing agency. \n8. The entire issue is required to be examined which certainly \naffects the future of large number of candidates, who are eligible,\nand qualified and are in queue for waiting their appointments. If \nthe Government Order provides that only after sending the \nrequisition for recruitment on regular basis and on an eventuality \nof delay of selection process, for the time being appointment can \nbe made through outsourcing agency, then the question is how\nwithout sending requisition large number of appointments were \nmade through outsource agencies. \n9. Learned State Counsel also informs to this Court that \nlearned Advocate General had also sent a proposal to the \nGovernment for framing Scheme as one time measure for \nregularizing the out sourced employees, who are working since \nlast more than 10 years. \n10. Let affidavit be filed by the Secretary, Karmik, Government \nof Uttarakhand, to answer the queries framed in earlier order\nwithin three weeks positively along with present queries within \nthree weeks. He shall also disclose whether any decision has been \ntaken on the proposal sent by the learned Advocate General. \n11. Put up this matter on 30.12.2024.\n (Rakesh Thapliyal, J.)\n 04.12.2024\nSKS"},{"date":"2025-01-08","judge":"Hon'ble Mr. Justice Rakesh Thapliyal","kind":"order","text":"SL. \nNo Date\nOffice Notes, \nreports, orders \nor proceedings or \ndirections and \nRegistrar’s order \nwith Signatures\nCOURT’S OR JUDGES’S ORDERS\nWPSS No. 2128 of 2024\nHon’ble Rakesh Thapliyal, J.\n1. Mr. K.K. Joshi, learned counsel for the \npetitioners and Mr. P.S. Bisht, learned Additional \nChief Standing Counsel for the State.\n2. List this matter in the last week of \nMarch, 2025.\n(Rakesh Thapliyal, J.)\n 08.01.2025\nUjjwal\f "}]}